.TH mknod 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
mknod \- create a device node or FIFO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mknod
.I path
.BR b | c
.I "major minor"
.br
.B mknod
.I path
.B p
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mknod
creates a special file.
.B b
makes a block device,
.B c
a character device and
.B p
a FIFO.  Block and character devices need the
.I major
and
.I minor
numbers; a FIFO takes neither.
.PP
The node is created with mode 0777 less the current
.BR umask ,
so set the mode afterwards with
.BR chmod (1)
if it should not be world writable.
.SH EXAMPLES
The nodes /etc/rc expects are made when the card is built; these are the
forms it uses.
.nf
# mknod /dev/tty1 c 5 1
# mknod /dev/hda1 b 0 1
.fi
.SH NOTES
Only the superuser may create a device node.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfifo (1),
.BR chmod (1),
.BR mount (1)
